---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Infrastructure status
description: Status of WA amateur radio infrastructure (AllStar hubs, repeaters, wireless links, digipeaters, beacons, gateways, receivers and sites), live AllStar linking, current issues, and how to report a fault. Demonstration.
permalink: /get-on-air/infrastructure/
scripts: [/assets/js/infrastructure.js]
---
{%- set I = infrastructure %}
{%- set LABEL = { up: "On air", degraded: "Degraded", down: "Off air", maintenance: "Maintenance", unknown: "Unknown" } %}
{%- set PLURAL = { Hub: "AllStar hubs", Repeater: "Repeaters", Link: "Wireless links", "Internet link": "Internet links", Digipeater: "APRS digipeaters", Beacon: "Beacons", Gateway: "Internet gateways", Receiver: "Online receivers", Power: "Site power", Site: "Sites" } %}
<header class="page-head">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Get on air · Infrastructure</p>
    <h1>Infrastructure status</h1>
    <p class="lede">The repeaters, linking hubs, wireless links, digipeaters, beacons, gateways and sites that keep WA on the air: what's working, what's being worked on, and how to tell the keeper when something's wrong.</p>
    <p class="notice demo-note"><b>Demonstration.</b> The AllStar hubs and the repeaters on them are real, with live linking status from AllStarLink. VK6RB Shenton Ridge is real. Rows tagged <span class="tag tag-sample">sample</span> are made up to show how the board could work. Check details with the keeper before relying on them.</p>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap infra-page">
  <ul class="infra-summary" aria-label="Status summary">
    {%- for s in ["up", "degraded", "down", "maintenance", "unknown"] %}
    <li class="st-{{ s }}"><b>{{ I.counts[s] }}</b><span><i class="dot"></i>{{ LABEL[s] }}</span></li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>

  <section class="card" style="--bar: var(--coral)" aria-labelledby="issues-h">
    <h2 id="issues-h">Current issues <small>{{ I.open.length }} open</small></h2>
    <ul class="issue-list">
      {%- for i in I.open %}
      <li class="issue sev-{{ i.Severity }}" id="issue-{{ i.Id }}">
        <div class="issue-head">
          <span class="state">{{ i.State }}</span>
          <b>{{ i.item.Title }}</b>{% if i.item.Sample %} <span class="tag tag-sample">sample</span>{% endif %}
          <span class="muted small">{% if i.item.Sub %}{{ i.item.Sub }} · {% endif %}{{ i.item.Type }} · #{{ i.Id }} · opened {{ i.Opened | shortDate }}</span>
        </div>
        <p class="issue-title">{{ i.Title }}</p>
        <p class="issue-update"><span class="muted">Latest, {{ i.Updated | shortDate }}:</span> {{ i.Update }}</p>
      </li>
      {%- else %}
      <li class="muted">No open issues. Everything's on air.</li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card" style="--bar: var(--accent)" aria-labelledby="links-h" id="allstar">
    <h2 id="links-h">Linked networks <small>AllStar, live</small></h2>
    <p class="allstar-summary" aria-live="polite"><span class="muted">Checking the AllStar hubs…</span></p>
    <div class="hub-grid">
      {%- for h in I.hubs %}
      <article class="hub-card" data-hub="{{ h.node }}">
        <header><b>{{ h.title }}</b><span class="muted small">{% if h.sub %}{{ h.sub }} · {% endif %}AllStar {{ h.node }}</span><span class="hub-state muted small">…</span></header>
        <div class="hub-body"><p class="small muted">Live status loads from AllStarLink.</p></div>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="small muted">Live from <a href="https://stats.allstarlink.org/" rel="noopener">AllStarLink</a>, refreshed every minute while this page is open. Personal hotspots are counted, not named. <a href="{{ '/get-on-air/infrastructure/allstar-live/' | url }}">Open the full live dashboard (Allmon3)</a>.</p>
    <script type="application/json" id="allstar-data">{{ { hubs: I.hubs, nodes: I.nodes } | dump | safe }}</script>
  </section>

  <section class="card infra-card" style="--bar: var(--navy)" aria-labelledby="list-h">
    <h2 id="list-h">Everything we track <small>{{ I.total }} items</small></h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
    <table class="infra-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Item</th><th>Details</th><th>Connects / serves</th><th>Checked</th><th><span class="sr-only">Report</span></th></tr></thead>
      {%- for g in I.groups %}
      <tbody>
        <tr class="group"><th colspan="6" scope="rowgroup">{{ PLURAL[g.type] or g.type }} <span>{{ g.items.length }}</span></th></tr>
        {%- for r in g.items %}
        <tr class="st-{{ r.Status }}">
          <td data-label="Status"><span class="status"><i class="dot"></i>{{ LABEL[r.Status] }}</span></td>
          <td data-label="Item"><b>{{ r.Title }}</b>{% if r.Sample %} <span class="tag tag-sample">sample</span>{% endif %}<span class="sub">{% if r.Sub %}{{ r.Sub }} · {% endif %}{% if r.site %}at {{ r.site.Name }}{% else %}{{ r.Region }}{% endif %}{% for i in r.issues %} · <a href="#issue-{{ i.Id }}">issue #{{ i.Id }}</a>{% endfor %}</span></td>
          <td data-label="Details" class="detail">{{ r.Detail }}</td>
          <td data-label="Connects">{% if r.AllStar %}AllStar {{ r.AllStar }}{% if r.hub %}<span class="sub">usually on {{ r.hub.Title }}</span>{% endif %}<span class="live-link" data-node="{{ r.AllStar }}"{% if r.hub %} data-expect="{{ r.hub.AllStar }}"{% endif %}{% if r.Type == "Hub" %} data-is-hub{% endif %}></span>{% elif r.onSite.length %}On site: {{ r.onSite | join(", ") }}{% else %}{{ r.Connects or "–" }}{% endif %}</td>
          <td data-label="Checked" class="small nowrap">{{ r.Checked | shortDate }}</td>
          <td><button class="button ghost small-btn" type="button" data-report="{{ r.Id }}">Report</button></td>
        </tr>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tbody>
      {%- endfor %}
    </table>
    </div>
    <p class="small muted">"Checked" is the last time someone confirmed the status. A fault at a site takes down everything on it, so sites are listed too. AllStar links are checked live: "Not linked" means the node isn't connected to any of the hubs right now.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="infra-two">
    <section class="card" style="--bar: var(--accent)" aria-labelledby="report-h">
      <h2 id="report-h">Report a problem</h2>
      <p>A repeater that won't open, a link that's dropping out, a silent beacon, or something working again after a quiet spell? Tell its keeper. Reports from several stations help pin a fault down.</p>
      <p><button class="button" type="button" data-report="">Report an issue</button></p>
      <p class="small muted">Say where you were and what you were running: "Handheld, Rockingham, can't open it" is more useful than "it's broken".</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card" style="--bar: var(--green)" aria-labelledby="resolved-h">
      <h2 id="resolved-h">Recently fixed</h2>
      <ul class="issue-list compact">
        {%- for i in I.resolved %}
        <li><b>{{ i.item.Title }}</b> <span class="muted small">{{ i.Updated | shortDate }}</span><br><span class="small">{{ i.Title }}. {{ i.Update }}</span></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="card" style="--bar: var(--gold)" aria-labelledby="how-h">
    <h2 id="how-h" class="on-gold">How it would work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Keepers update their own items</b>, from a simple form or a shared Sheet. The page rebuilds itself with the rest of vk6.net.</li>
      <li><b>Reports go straight to the keeper</b> of that item, with a copy kept so the next person can see it's already known.</li>
      <li><b>Linking is checked live.</b> Each repeater records the hub it normally sits on, and the board flags it the moment it drops off.</li>
      <li><b>Sites know what's on them</b>, so a power failure at a hilltop shows every repeater and link it takes down.</li>
      <li><b>Anyone can confirm something is working</b>, which keeps "Checked" fresh for remote sites nobody hears often.</li>
      <li>Later: alerts for the items you use, and planned work shown on <a href="{{ '/whats-on/' | url }}">What's on</a>.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</div>

<dialog class="infra-dialog" id="report-dialog" aria-labelledby="rd-title">
  <form method="dialog">
    <h2 id="rd-title">Report an issue</h2>
    <label>Which item?
      <select name="item" required>
        <option value="">Choose a repeater, link, beacon…</option>
        {%- for g in I.groups %}<optgroup label="{{ PLURAL[g.type] or g.type }}">{% for r in g.items | sort(false, false, "Title") %}<option value="{{ r.Id }}">{{ r.Title }}{% if r.Sub %} ({{ r.Sub }}){% endif %}</option>{% endfor %}</optgroup>{% endfor %}
      </select>
    </label>
    <fieldset>
      <legend>What's happening?</legend>
      <label class="opt"><input type="radio" name="kind" value="off" required> Off air / no response</label>
      <label class="opt"><input type="radio" name="kind" value="quality"> Poor audio, weak or dropping out</label>
      <label class="opt"><input type="radio" name="kind" value="link"> Link or internet connection not working</label>
      <label class="opt"><input type="radio" name="kind" value="interference"> Interference or a stuck carrier</label>
      <label class="opt"><input type="radio" name="kind" value="working"> It's working fine (confirm status)</label>
      <label class="opt"><input type="radio" name="kind" value="other"> Something else</label>
    </fieldset>
    <label>Details <span class="muted small">where you were, radio and antenna, when</span>
      <textarea name="details" rows="3"></textarea>
    </label>
    <div class="rd-row">
      <label>Your callsign <input name="call" autocomplete="off" placeholder="VK6…"></label>
      <label>Email <span class="muted small">optional, for a reply</span> <input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email"></label>
    </div>
    <p class="rd-done notice" hidden><b>Thanks! This is a demonstration,</b> so nothing was sent. On the real board this would go to the item's keeper.</p>
    <div class="rd-actions">
      <button class="button ghost" type="button" data-close>Close</button>
      <button class="button" type="submit">Send report</button>
    </div>
  </form>
</dialog>
